{"_meta":{"as_of":"2026-11-13T21:49:38+00:00","coverage":"7/7","note":"Earnings dates and consensus from Yahoo Finance \u2014 often estimated rather than company-confirmed, so treat them as approximate until close. Policy and catalyst entries are hand-dated in the research files."},"events":[{"d":"2026-07-28","type":"policy","t":"LIVE \u2014 FCC Covered List now bars foreign-produced robots (Jul 28, 2026)","why":"Adopted, not proposed. Any ground-moving device over 4.4lb (with dock) that senses, connects and navigates cannot get FCC equipment authorisation unless the Department of War grants a Conditional Approval. Read the carve-outs before pricing it: industrial robotic ARMS, medical robots, vehicles and drones are explicitly excluded, so Fanuc, Yaskawa, ABB, KUKA/Midea, Estun and Doosan's cobots are untouched. What is caught is humanoids, quadrupeds and autonomous mobile robots \u2014 9880.HK UBTech head-on, 277810.KQ Rainbow Robotics and TER's MiR unit on the same terms despite being allied, plus 1810.HK Xiaomi's consumer line. HSAI is hit second-hand through its customers' US market access. The asymmetry is the point: US-produced humanoids get a market cleared by rule, everyone else queues for a discretionary exemption.","hits":"act, sen"},{"d":"2026-08-04","type":"policy","t":"Chinese WFE tools qualifying at Samsung and SK Hynix","why":"Reuters, Aug 4 2026: both Korean memory makers have been testing AMEC etch tools for their China fabs \u2014 begun ~2 years ago, aimed at SERVICING and upgrading existing lines rather than adding capacity, after Washington revoked their validated-end-user status in 2025 and replaced it with an annual licence. Small in units, large in meaning: qualification is the slow half of the WFE moat, and it is being done by the two customers whose sign-off other buyers copy. Deutsche Bank has NAURA, AMEC, Piotech and ACM Research each clearing $1B of revenue in 2026 and together taking 25-30% of China's ~$28B WFE market. This is the external bear case (see Thesis) arriving as an event rather than an opinion \u2014 watch whether qualification stays confined to China fabs.","hits":"wfe"},{"d":"2026-09-30","type":"catalyst","t":"800-volt DC racks \u2014 first volume shipments","why":"Opens the SiC/GaN power-chip story: Infineon, onsemi, Navitas, Delta, Lite-On.","hits":"Power & Cooling"},{"d":"2026-09-30","type":"catalyst","t":"Unitree IPO prices on the STAR board","why":"The first real public-market test of humanoid-maker economics.","hits":"Humanoid Robotics"},{"d":"2026-10-15","type":"catalyst","t":"TSMC Q3 report \u2014 does capex fear break?","why":"The best sentiment gauge for the whole AI supply chain \u2014 and the catalyst on our #1 entry window.","hits":"Foundry & Packaging"},{"d":"2026-10-27","type":"catalyst","t":"SK Hynix Q3: delayed HBM4 revenue lands","why":"The catalyst on our #2 entry window: confirms or breaks the 'repriced, not broken' read.","hits":"Memory (HBM)"},{"d":"2026-11-05","type":"earnings","tk":"5274.TWO","n":"ASPEED Technology","conv":3,"froth":2,"eps":71.41,"eps_lo":42.31,"eps_hi":55.03,"dd":-39.0,"ts":1793856600,"when":"post","xt":"13:30 CST"},{"d":"2026-11-05","type":"earnings","tk":"AKAM","n":"Akamai","conv":2,"froth":1,"eps":1.62,"eps_lo":1.52,"eps_hi":1.74,"dd":-46.2,"ts":1793912400,"when":"post","xt":"16:00 EST","rep":{"act":1.77,"est":1.67,"when":"2026-11-05","surp":5.8,"move":-0.14,"live":true,"post":0.3}},{"d":"2026-11-05","type":"earnings","tk":"HIMX","n":"Himax Technologies","conv":2,"froth":2,"eps":0.22,"eps_lo":0.22,"eps_hi":0.22,"dd":-61.8,"ts":1793885400,"when":"pre","xt":"08:30 EST","rep":{"act":0.11,"est":0.09,"when":"2026-11-05","surp":18.9,"move":-1.43,"live":true,"post":0.9}},{"d":"2026-11-05","type":"earnings","tk":"LR.PA","n":"Legrand","conv":1,"froth":2,"eps":1.75,"eps_lo":1.64,"eps_hi":1.83,"dd":-12.0,"ts":1793896200,"when":"post","xt":"17:30 CET","rep":{"act":1.5,"est":1.49,"when":"2026-11-04","surp":0.7,"move":-0.32,"live":true}},{"d":"2026-11-0