r every 'Western winner' still runs through China","why":"Worth holding against any policy-beneficiary trade in this map. OPTICS: every transceiver laser is built on an indium phosphide substrate, InP has been under Chinese export control since 2025, and it has no substitute at these speeds. Lumentum's CEO has called the InP shortage worse than the memory crunch; AXTI's backlog is >$100M into 2027, and AXTI itself produces in China under the same permit system. The May-Jun 2026 permit easing was selective and politically contingent, not structural. ROBOTICS: a US-built humanoid still needs NdFeB magnets, and the truce covering them expires Nov 10 2026. So a name can win the market-access argument by rule and still lose the input argument by permit. Raw-material depth lives in the Hard Assets sibling map \u2014 what belongs here is the conclusion: onshored assembly does not equal an onshored supply chain.","hits":"opt, act"},{"d":"2026-11-10","type":"policy","t":"Nov 10, 2026 \u2014 China rare-earth truce expires","why":"Renewal = status quo; lapse = magnets/Ga/Ge/chemicals shock into robotics, optics and fab chemicals. The single most dated policy risk on the board.","hits":"act, opt, wfe"},{"d":"2026-11-10","type":"catalyst","t":"China rare-earth truce: renew or lapse (Nov 10)","why":"A dated, binary event under the robotics, optics and fab-chemical chains \u2014 position sizing should know the date.","hits":"Policy & Fiscal"},{"d":"2026-11-10","type":"earnings","tk":"3017.TW","n":"Asia Vital Components","conv":2,"froth":2,"eps":34.42,"eps_lo":24.83,"eps_hi":29.7,"dd":-17.2,"ts":1794288600,"when":"post","xt":"13:30 CST","rep":{"act":29.32,"est":28.01,"when":"2026-11-10","surp":4.7,"move":9.91,"live":true},"wire":{"cues":[],"heads":[{"t":"Asia Vital Components Co., Ltd. Earnings Call - November 10, 2026","u":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMigAFBVV95cUxNeU5CSDBuSmpTNjdzUmh0Qk1pbWRuZndYNTVrZS03cVVxdUt4Y0RLdDdYYnJLRU5zb0hpdEhiYTZQT25sem1VNlZvSm43cHRUdlBRand1TV